    "message": {
     "content": "### The Verdict: **You should strongly lean toward accepting this offer.**\n\nYour pushback worked effectively. Securing a **$200,000 cash sign-on bonus** on top of a matched $240,000 base and a $1.08M equity grant is top-of-market for a Google L6 PM. \n\nBy giving you $200k in upfront cash to offset your next 12 months of unvested Meta RSUs, Google effectively **paid you twice** for that equity: you get $200,000 in immediate cash *and* your full $1,080,000 new-hire grant.\n\n---\n\n### Total Compensation Comparison\n\n| Year | Meta (Estimated) | Google (Standard 33/33/22/12 Vesting)* | Google (Flat 25% Vesting) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Year 1** | ~$526,000 | **~$844,400** (+$318k vs Meta) | **~$758,000** (+$232k vs Meta) |\n| **Year 2** | ~$550,000 | **~$707,000** (+$157k vs Meta) | **~$621,000** (+$71k vs Meta) |\n| **Year 3** | ~$575,000 | **~$651,000** (+$76k vs Meta) | **~$646,000** (+$71k vs Meta) |\n| **Year 4** | ~$600,000 | **~$605,000** (Parity) | **~$671,000** (+$71k vs Meta) |\n| **4-Yr Total**| **~$2.25M** | **~$2.81M** | **~$2.70M** |\n\n*\\*Note: Google\u2019s standard equity schedule vests 33% in Yr 1, 33% in Yr 2, 22% in Yr 3, and 12% in Yr 4. Calculations for Years 2\u20134 assume target performance refreshers (~$250k/4-yr grants) stack as described by the recruiter.*\n\n#### Key Financial Takeaways:\n1. **Massive Year 1 & 2 Windfall:** You lock in an extra **~$450,000\u2013$500,000 in total compensation over your first two years** compared to staying at Meta.\n2. **Guaranteed Cash Surplus:** The $200,000 sign-on is liquid cash, completely eliminating market volatility risk on the equity you are leaving behind at Meta.\n\n---\n\n### 3 Details to Verify Before Signing\n\nBefore you put pen to paper, ask the recruiter to confirm these operational points in writing:\n\n1. **Sign-on Bonus Disbursement & Clawback:**\n   * *When is it paid?* Typically paid in your first or second paycheck. Confirm whether it is paid 100% upfront or split across Year 1 and Year 2 (e.g., $100k / $100k).\n   * *Clawback terms:* Confirm if the clawback period is 12 or 24 months, and whether it is prorated monthly if you leave voluntarily before that time.\n2. **Equity Vesting Schedule:**\n   * Confirm that the grant is on Google's standard front-loaded schedule (**33% / 33% / 22% / 12%**). This front-loading is a major benefit to you.\n3. **Start Date & Meta Bonus Alignment:**\n   * Ensure your start date allows you to collect any earned bonus/vesting events at Meta if you are within weeks of a payout date.\n\n---\n\n### Non-Financial Factors to Weigh\n\nIf you decide to turn this down, it should be strictly for **career/cultural reasons**, not compensation:\n\n* **Promotion Velocity (L6 $\\rightarrow$ L7 vs IC6 $\\rightarrow$ IC7):** Meta generally moves faster on promotions for high performers, while Google\u2019s L7 PM promotion process can take longer and involve more committee bureaucracy.\n* **Execution vs Consensus:** Meta\u2019s culture tends to favor autonomous execution (\"move fast\"), whereas Google PM culture often requires building broader stakeholder consensus.\n* **Scope & Product Alignment:** Ensure the specific product area and team at Google in SF excites you more than your current scope at Meta.\n\n### Final Recommendation\n**Accept the offer.** Google has stretched to the top of their L6 band to win you over. The guaranteed Year 1 cash/equity upside more than compensates for the transition friction.",
